id: pm-rl-et5b
title: "Environment registration and versioning, immutable once referenced"
description: "An Environment holds the task suite, reward specification, and version as content-addressed project context. Registration is idempotent by canonical content, changed content receives a new id, and every pm-rl command revalidates the stored hash before use. Arbitrary direct core mutations cannot yet be intercepted at write time; host-level mutation guards remain pending pm-cli#854, so this feature stays in progress until the SDK exposes that capability."
type: Feature
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:30.856Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T23:49:26.817Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Registering a changed reward specification against a referenced version is refused and produces a new version instead; every Run records the exact environment version id it ran against; show reports the reward specification that was in force
release: 2026.7.31
blocked_reason: "Externally blocked on pm-cli#854: the 2026.8.1 extension SDK has no pre-commit mutation guard, so arbitrary direct core mutations cannot be intercepted at write time. The feature stays blocked until the SDK exposes that capability."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rl-e20d,parent,"2026-07-31T06:38:31.227Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T12:07:57.787Z",codex,"Registration now derives `Environment` ids from canonical specification content, is byte-idempotent, produces a new id for any changed reward spec, stores the human version plus full hash, and verifies body/hash/id consistency before every Run snapshot. Every Run records the exact environment id and copies the exact specification into its immutable start body. Direct arbitrary core mutations still cannot be rejected at write time because the 2026.8.1 extension SDK has no pre-commit mutation guard; tracked upstream as https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/854. The feature remains in progress until that host capability exists. Related host integration gaps found and worked around without doubles: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/853 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/855."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,Content-addressed registration and provenance snapshot
tests[2]{command,scope}:
  "name=a changed reward specification registers as a new version rather than overwriting the referenced one,result=pass",project
  "name=an environment registers idempotently by canonical content and can be listed and shown,result=pass",project
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  README.md,project,Current enforcement boundary
